[SIZE=5][B]4. Zero-Dependency Backend Bridge & NPCs[/B][/SIZE]

Unlike other navigators requiring separate plugins or Citizens, VelocityNavigator is completely self-contained:

[LIST]
[*][B]Single Universal JAR:[/B] The exact same JAR file placed on Velocity runs on Paper, Spigot, and Folia backends.
[*][B]Zero-NMS Packet NPCs:[/B] Spawn lightweight NPCs without version-locked NMS code. Compatible across Paper 1.16.5-1.21.x and Folia out of the box. Fetch player skins, configure click actions (server connect, open menu, dispatch commands), and manage in-game via /vn npc.
[*][B]Backend YAML Menus (plugins/VelocityNavigator/menus/*.yml):[/B] Build custom inventory menus on backends without third-party GUI plugins. Supports custom model data, skull owners, sounds, and multi-actions.
[*][B]PlaceholderAPI Bridge:[/B] Access proxy values (%velocitynavigator_lobby%, %velocitynavigator_party_leader%, %velocitynavigator_server_status_<server>%) on backends.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DemonZ-Development/VelocityNavigator/main/assets/marketplace/05-optional-systems.png[/IMG][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]5. Built-in Proxy Systems & Social Features[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Capacity Queue System:[/B] Never turn players away during surges. Hold incoming players in a holding server with actionbar and title countdowns. Priority bypass permissions for VIPs.
[*][B]Cross-Server Party System:[/B] Full party management (/party create, invite, join, leave, kick, disband). Leader Follow transfers all party members automatically when the leader switches servers.
[*][B]Network & Per-Server Maintenance:[/B] Lock individual servers or the entire network with custom kick reasons and dynamic MOTD badges.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]6. Multi-Proxy Clustering & Redis Sync[/B][/SIZE]

Running multiple Velocity proxies behind BGP Anycast or DNS round-robin?
[LIST]
[*]Cross-proxy health and circuit state synchronization in milliseconds
[*]Cluster-wide sticky sessions and player affinity across all proxies
[*]Dynamic server auto-registration over Redis Pub/Sub
[*]Authenticated, channel-isolated communication
[/LIST]

[CENTER][IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DemonZ-Development/VelocityNavigator/main/assets/marketplace/08-defensive-design.png[/IMG][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]7. Enterprise Security & Authentication Engine[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Argon2id Password Hashing:[/B] State-of-the-art password security with configurable memory cost and backward-compatible SHA-256 verification.
[*][B]Brute-Force Rate Limiting:[/B] Login attempt tracking and temporary IP lockouts stop password guessing attacks.
[*][B]Holding Lobby Quarantine:[/B] Unauthenticated players are isolated in a holding lobby with movement, interaction, and chat restricted until login.
[*][B]Native Bedrock Auth Forms:[/B] Bedrock players receive native modal dialogs instead of typing passwords in open chat.
[*][B]Expiring Session Tokens:[/B] Secure session persistence remembers players across quick reconnects.
[/LIST]

